IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cards-domain`

§ `Arithmetic and answer-building shared by the issuer modules`

-- ===========================================================================
-- A SECOND SHARED MODULE, BESIDE THE ONTOLOGY, AND WHY.
-- The ontology module is nouns only. Four small pieces of machinery are the
-- same in every issuer module and would otherwise be typed fourteen times and
-- drift: rounding down to a multiple, building an `Earn answer`, reading a
-- MAYBE MCC, and merging a worst-case and a best-case evaluation into one
-- answer with a floor and a ceiling. Nothing here states a rate, a cap or an
-- exclusion; those are the issuers' and live in the issuer modules. This is
-- an engineering decision of the encoder's, not a ruling (NOTES.md,
-- "Assumed, not ruled").
--
-- THE FLOOR AND THE CEILING. Where a purchase waits on a fact the cardholder
-- cannot yet state (an MCC she has not seen, an indicator the acquirer has not
-- sent, a month-end condition), an issuer module evaluates the purchase
-- twice, once on the worst reading of the unknown and once on the best, and
-- `bracketed from ... to ... with ...` joins the two. The floor is the worst
-- evaluation's `units certain`, the ceiling the best evaluation's
-- `units at best`, and the conditions are named only when the two differ.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Rounding`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, unit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to a multiple of` n unit MEANS
    (FLOOR (n DIVIDED BY unit)) TIMES unit

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded down to a whole number` n MEANS
    FLOOR n

-- Never negative: a cap that is already over-spent leaves room 0, not less.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`at least nothing` n MEANS
    max n 0


§§ `UOB's "per S$5" rewards, on two readings`

-- UOB writes every rate as "UNI$X for every S$5". Reading 1 (whole blocks,
-- fork F-uob-per-five): only each complete S$5 earns,
-- so S$4.99 earns nothing and S$9 earns as S$5. Reading 2 (pro rata): the
-- rate is X/5 per dollar. Both then round the transaction's UNI$ down to a
-- whole figure (VS cl.4(i); PRVI cl.1(iv)). The two agree on every multiple of
-- S$5. The UOB modules take Reading 1 as the floor, Reading 2 as the ceiling,
-- and name the open reading when they differ. ASSUMED, NOT RULED.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, perFive IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`UNI$ by whole S$5 blocks` amount perFive MEANS
    FLOOR ((FLOOR (amount DIVIDED BY 5)) TIMES perFive)

GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER, perFive IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`UNI$ pro rata` amount perFive MEANS
    FLOOR ((amount TIMES perFive) DIVIDED BY 5)


§§ `Reading a MAYBE category code`

-- TRUE iff she knows the code and it is in the list. An unknown code is not in
-- any list: callers that need the other reading evaluate again with a stand-in.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, codes IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the code is among` p codes MEANS
    CONSIDER p's mcc
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN elem n codes

GIVEN p IS A Purchase, low IS A NUMBER, high IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the code is from` p low high MEANS
    CONSIDER p's mcc
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN n AT LEAST low AND n AT MOST high

GIVEN p IS A Purchase
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the code is unknown for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's mcc
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST n  THEN FALSE

-- The same purchase with a stand-in code, for the worst-case and best-case
-- evaluations. Only the code changes.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, code IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Purchase
`recoded purchase` p code MEANS
    Purchase WITH
        `amount in SGD`      IS p's `amount in SGD`
        `date charged`       IS p's `date charged`
        `date posted`        IS p's `date posted`
        `posting status`     IS p's `posting status`
        `charge kind`        IS p's `charge kind`
        currency             IS p's currency
        gateway              IS p's gateway
        `store location`     IS p's `store location`
        presentation         IS p's presentation
        `merchant indicator` IS p's `merchant indicator`
        merchant             IS p's merchant
        outlet               IS p's outlet
        item                 IS p's item
        mcc                  IS JUST code
        descriptor           IS p's descriptor
        `later reversed`     IS p's `later reversed`

-- The same purchase with a stand-in indicator.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, flag IS A `Merchant indicator`
GIVETH A Purchase
`reflagged purchase` p flag MEANS
    Purchase WITH
        `amount in SGD`      IS p's `amount in SGD`
        `date charged`       IS p's `date charged`
        `date posted`        IS p's `date posted`
        `posting status`     IS p's `posting status`
        `charge kind`        IS p's `charge kind`
        currency             IS p's currency
        gateway              IS p's gateway
        `store location`     IS p's `store location`
        presentation         IS p's presentation
        `merchant indicator` IS flag
        merchant             IS p's merchant
        outlet               IS p's outlet
        item                 IS p's item
        mcc                  IS p's mcc
        descriptor           IS p's descriptor
        `later reversed`     IS p's `later reversed`

-- The same purchase with a stand-in gateway.
GIVEN p IS A Purchase, gate IS A Gateway
GIVETH A Purchase
`rerouted purchase` p gate MEANS
    Purchase WITH
        `amount in SGD`      IS p's `amount in SGD`
        `date charged`       IS p's `date charged`
        `date posted`        IS p's `date posted`
        `posting status`     IS p's `posting status`
        `charge kind`        IS p's `charge kind`
        currency             IS p's currency
        gateway              IS gate
        `store location`     IS p's `store location`
        presentation         IS p's presentation
        `merchant indicator` IS p's `merchant indicator`
        merchant             IS p's merchant
        outlet               IS p's outlet
        item                 IS p's item
        mcc                  IS p's mcc
        descriptor           IS p's descriptor
        `later reversed`     IS p's `later reversed`


§§ `Building an answer`

GIVEN c IS A Card
      cur IS A `Reward currency`
      certain IS A NUMBER
      best IS A NUMBER
      wanted IS A NUMBER
      perUnit IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      excl IS A BOOLEAN
      thePot IS A Pot
      deps IS A LIST OF Condition
      cl IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`an answer for` c `in` cur `of` certain `to` best `wanting` wanted `at` perUnit `excluded` excl `drawing on` thePot `depending on` deps `per` cl MEANS
    `Earn answer` WITH
        card                     IS c
        `reward currency`        IS cur
        `units certain`          IS certain
        `units at best`          IS best
        `bonus units before cap` IS wanted
        `miles certain`          IS `miles from units` certain perUnit
        `miles at best`          IS `miles from units` best perUnit
        `cash value certain`     IS NOTHING
        `cash value at best`     IS NOTHING
        excluded                 IS excl
        pot                      IS thePot
        `depends on`             IS deps
        clause                   IS cl

GIVEN units IS A NUMBER, perUnit IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`miles from units` units perUnit MEANS
    CONSIDER perUnit
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST k  THEN JUST (units TIMES k)

-- An answer that earns nothing for a stated reason.
GIVEN c IS A Card, cur IS A `Reward currency`, cl IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`nothing is earned on` c `in` cur `per` cl MEANS
    `an answer for` c `in` cur `of` 0 `to` 0 `wanting` 0 `at` (JUST 0) `excluded` TRUE `drawing on` `No pot` `depending on` EMPTY `per` cl


-- The same answer with a Singapore-dollar cash value per unit, for the
-- cash-rebate programmes (the Smart card, the yuu Point).
GIVEN ans IS AN `Earn answer`
      dollarsPerUnit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the answer` ans `valued in dollars at` dollarsPerUnit MEANS
    `Earn answer` WITH
        card                     IS ans's card
        `reward currency`        IS ans's `reward currency`
        `units certain`          IS ans's `units certain`
        `units at best`          IS ans's `units at best`
        `bonus units before cap` IS ans's `bonus units before cap`
        `miles certain`          IS ans's `miles certain`
        `miles at best`          IS ans's `miles at best`
        `cash value certain`     IS JUST ((ans's `units certain`) TIMES dollarsPerUnit)
        `cash value at best`     IS JUST ((ans's `units at best`) TIMES dollarsPerUnit)
        excluded                 IS ans's excluded
        pot                      IS ans's pot
        `depends on`             IS ans's `depends on`
        clause                   IS ans's clause


-- Two answers for the same purchase that add: a card's own earn plus an uplift
-- that a second document grants on top of it (the Lady's Savings Account
-- uplift on the Lady's card). Units add; miles and cash add only where both
-- sides state them; the conditions join; the pot is the first answer's.
GIVEN first IS AN `Earn answer`
      second IS AN `Earn answer`
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`the answers added` first second MEANS
    `Earn answer` WITH
        card                     IS first's card
        `reward currency`        IS first's `reward currency`
        `units certain`          IS (first's `units certain`) PLUS (second's `units certain`)
        `units at best`          IS (first's `units at best`) PLUS (second's `units at best`)
        `bonus units before cap` IS (first's `bonus units before cap`) PLUS (second's `bonus units before cap`)
        `miles certain`          IS `the maybe sum of` (first's `miles certain`) (second's `miles certain`)
        `miles at best`          IS `the maybe sum of` (first's `miles at best`) (second's `miles at best`)
        `cash value certain`     IS `the maybe sum of` (first's `cash value certain`) (second's `cash value certain`)
        `cash value at best`     IS `the maybe sum of` (first's `cash value at best`) (second's `cash value at best`)
        excluded                 IS (first's excluded) AND (second's excluded)
        pot                      IS first's pot
        `depends on`             IS nub (append (first's `depends on`) (second's `depends on`))
        clause                   IS first's clause

GIVEN first IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      second IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the maybe sum of` first second MEANS
    CONSIDER first
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN
        CONSIDER second
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x PLUS y)


§§ `Joining the worst and the best evaluation`

-- The floor is the worst evaluation's certain units; the ceiling is the best
-- evaluation's best units. The named conditions appear only if the two differ,
-- so an answer that does not turn on the unknown does not name it.
GIVEN lo IS AN `Earn answer`
      hi IS AN `Earn answer`
      extra IS A LIST OF Condition
GIVETH A LIST OF Condition
`the conditions joining` lo hi extra MEANS
    IF lo's `units certain` EQUALS hi's `units at best`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE nub (append (append (lo's `depends on`) (hi's `depends on`)) extra)

GIVEN lo IS AN `Earn answer`
      hi IS AN `Earn answer`
      extra IS A LIST OF Condition
GIVETH AN `Earn answer`
`bracketed from` lo `to` hi `adding` extra MEANS
    `Earn answer` WITH
        card                     IS hi's card
        `reward currency`        IS hi's `reward currency`
        `units certain`          IS lo's `units certain`
        `units at best`          IS hi's `units at best`
        `bonus units before cap` IS hi's `bonus units before cap`
        `miles certain`          IS lo's `miles certain`
        `miles at best`          IS hi's `miles at best`
        `cash value certain`     IS lo's `cash value certain`
        `cash value at best`     IS hi's `cash value at best`
        excluded                 IS lo's excluded AND hi's excluded
        pot                      IS hi's pot
        `depends on`             IS `the conditions joining` lo hi extra
        clause                   IS hi's clause

-- A flat 0 / 1 test used throughout.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if` b MEANS
    IF b THEN 1 ELSE 0
